export anchor NightFlightStyle:
    number: 414
    screen: TravelPlanner
    name: Night flight
    idea: The trip shown as a seatback screen in a darkened cabin, a deep violet bezel around a glowing moving map, swipeable itinerary tiles and a round icon dock, lit by a lavender and pink mood strip.
    base: dark
    palette:
        cabin: #0c0a18, the page, the cabin around the screen and the style sheet
        bezel: #050409, the rounded seatback frame
        screen: #141127, the map ground, dock buttons and secondary buttons
        panel: #1d1936, side panels and list rows
        line: #34305a, hairlines, the map grid and panel edges
        ink: #ece9ff, text and map labels
        muted: #aaa3d6, labels, meta and HUD captions
        mood: #b49cff, the primary button, the logo disc and icon tint
        onMood: #1a0f3d, text on the mood fill
        glow: #ff9ad5, the route arc, city dots, the blossom note and focus
        booked: #8ee6b8, Booked and Done text and icon on a dark green pill
        pending: #ffc98a, Not booked and To do text and icon on a dark amber pill
    type:
        One system stack, system-ui, Segoe UI, Roboto. Base 15px at 1.5. Big
        figures 44 to 48px at weight 200 with tabular numbers, the trip
        title 36px at 300, section titles 24px at 300, tile titles 19px at
        500, labels 12 to 13px caps tracked 0.1em in muted.
    layout:
        A cabin band with a soft violet ceiling glow and a thin lavender to
        pink light strip across the top. Centred in it a near black bezel
        with a 32px radius holds the whole screen. A top row has a lavender
        B disc with Brightwork Trips, the trip dates on the right and a pill
        Share trip button. Below, a two column grid. The wide left card is
        the moving map, a dark violet chart with a faint grid, an abstract
        coast, three pink city dots for Tokyo, Kyoto and Osaka joined by a
        dotted arc and a small white plane. The title Japan in April and
        Mara Okafor and one guest float on translucent chips over the map,
        and a HUD strip under it shows Route, Length 14 days and Stays
        booked 2 of 3. The right column stacks Budget with a 44px 3,200 and
        a lavender to pink glowing meter, Weather on arrival with a 48px 17
        degrees and a pink blossom line, and Before you fly with the four
        checks as pills. Under the grid, Itinerary is a sideways scrolling
        rail of six tall tiles, each with an icon disc, date, title, detail
        and a status pill. A dock of rounded icon buttons ends the screen,
        Book train filled in lavender. Below 900px the right column drops
        under the map, and at phone width the HUD cells stack.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 20px bezel padding, 16px between map and panels, 12px between tiles and 40px of cabin around the bezel.
    density: Low to medium. One large map, three side panels and one row of six tiles.
    corners: Very soft. A 32px bezel, a 24px map, 20px panels, 18px tiles and pills for chips and buttons.
    borders: A 1px violet line round every panel and tile, and between HUD cells.
    shadows: A deep black drop under the bezel with a faint lavender halo. The budget meter and the ceiling strip glow.
    icons:
        Rounded line icons at 1.8 stroke inside round tinted discs. Booked
        is a check circle, Not booked a dashed open circle, Done a checked
        box, To do an empty box and Flight a plane, each beside its word in
        a pill.
    focus: A 3px pink outline offset 3px, also round the scrolling tile rail.
    tone: Calm cabin announcements such as Before you fly, Weather on arrival and Itinerary.
